      "height": 4.95,
      "placeholder_type": "OBJECT",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "A family is walking along a Queensland beach which is not patrolled.  While wading through shallow water, a child in the family group steps on a stonefish. The child screams and collapses in pain.",
          "font_size": 28.0
        },
        {
          "text": "Three people are snorkelling off rocks near an open beach. One of them suffers a shallow-water blackout and is found floating unconscious in the water by the others.",
          "font_size": 28.0
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "slide-2": {
    "shape-0": {
      "left": 0.43,
      "top": 0.3,
      "width": 9.57,
      "height": 1.25,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Step 1: Identify the problem",
          "font_size": 48.0,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "FFFFFF"
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-1": {
      "left": 0.5,
      "top": 1.86,
      "width": 9.0,
      "height": 4.37,
      "placeholder_type": "OBJECT",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "How to respond to emergency situations on open beaches as quickly as possible. (An emergency could be in the water or on the beach.)",
          "font_size": 36.0
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "slide-3": {
    "shape-0": {
      "left": 0.22,
      "top": 0.13,
      "width": 9.57,
      "height": 1.25,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Step 2: Gather information",
          "font_size": 48.0,
          "bold": true
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-1": {
      "left": 0.5,
      "top": 1.75,
      "width": 9.0,
      "height": 4.95,
      "placeholder_type": "OBJECT",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Who needs to respond to emergencies? Ambulance, lifeguards, fire brigade, SES, council employees",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": "What information do they need to know?  Location of emergency, number of people involved, level of consciousness of casualties, injuries to casualties, treatment of casualties, ease of access: roads, tracks, vegetation.",
          "bold": true
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "slide-4": {
    "shape-0": {
      "left": 0.43,
      "top": 0.3,
      "width": 9.57,
      "height": 1.25,
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Step 3: Ideas for possible solutions",
          "font_size": 48.0,
          "bold": true,
          "color": "FFFFFF"
        }
      ]
    },
    "shape-1": {
      "left": 0.5,
      "top": 1.78,
      "width": 9.0,
      "height": 5.39,
      "placeholder_type": "OBJECT",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Teach people first aid",
          "font_size": 28.0
        },
        {
          "text": "Put more lifesaving towers on beaches",
          "font_size": 28.0
        },
        {
          "text": "Have patrols on open beaches",
          "font_size": 28.0
        },
        {
          "text": "Have beach access signs with information",
          "font_size": 28.0
        },
        {
          "text": "Stop people from accessing open beaches",
          "font_size": 28.0
        },
        {
          "text": "Have special ambulances specifically for beach emergencies",
          "font_size": 28.0
        },
        {
          "text": "Have water-based responders",
          "font_size": 28.0
        },
        {
          "text": "Create more access roads to open beaches",
          "font_size": 28.0
        }
      ]
    }
  },
